# fine-tuned foundation-model forecaster checkpoints — regenerable from the
# committed seed-0 finetune scripts; too large for the free LFS quota
results/Heston/preprocessing_with_log_returns/forecaster/weights/*.pt
# TimeDiT 1M path-shadowing scenario bank — kept on disk only, NOT pushed
# (Theo's instruction). Regenerable via path_shadowing/gen_banks.py --variant raw;
# too large for the free LFS quota. Only ONE bank exists: TimeDiT's PS runs on the
# no-preproc checkpoint (preprocessing degrades it), so the bank lives under
# baseline_no_preproc/. The top-level path stays ignored as a safety net.
results/Heston/preprocessing_with_log_returns/TimeDiT/path_shadowing/bank/*.npy
results/Heston/preprocessing_with_log_returns/TimeDiT/baseline_no_preproc/path_shadowing/bank/*.npy
# TimeDiT model checkpoints — kept ON DISK in place (weights/seed_N_model.pt) so
# they stay accessible any time, but NOT pushed (Theo's instruction, 2026-07-31:
# "save the checkpoints inside the disk and do not push them ... they just do not
# appear in the github"). DiT-S is 32,512,897 fp32 params = 124.1 MiB per file,
# over GitHub's 100 MiB per-file HARD cap, and 7 files = 869 MiB would exhaust the
# free LFS tier (1 GiB) in a single push — see M10/M12.
# Regenerable: code/train_timedit_logret.py --seed N (deterministic).
# The small seed_N_config.json recipe files stay tracked.
results/Heston/preprocessing_with_log_returns/TimeDiT/weights/*.pt
results/Heston/preprocessing_with_log_returns/TimeDiT/baseline_no_preproc/weights/*.pt
# Experiment B regime oracle — ExtraTrees(500 trees, 77 features) serialises to
# 529 MiB, over GitHub's 100 MiB per-file HARD cap. The reproducible artefact is
# the gate accuracy in oracle/gate_report.json (tracked); the blob is refit locally
# via protocol/experiments/scripts/fit_heston_mixture_oracle.py --workers 16.
dataset/Heston/new_experiments/experiment_B/oracle/oracle.joblib
